# 9. Testbench

A **testbench** is used to check whether our Verilog design works correctly.

```text
             Testbench
                 │
                 │ gives inputs
                 ▼
           Full Adder RTL
                 │
                 │ produces outputs
                 ▼
             Waveform
                 │
                 ▼
       Compare with Truth Table
```

The testbench should test all 8 possible combinations:

```text
000
001
010
011
100
101
110
111
```

If the outputs match the truth table, our design is working correctly.

---

# 10. Simulation

The design is simulated using **Xilinx Vivado**.

### Simulation flow

```text
Verilog RTL
     ↓
Create Testbench
     ↓
Run Behavioral Simulation
     ↓
Observe SUM & CARRY
     ↓
Check Waveform
     ↓
Compare with Truth Table
     ↓
Design Verified ✓
```

The waveform should show the correct `SUM` and `CARRY` values for all input combinations.

